    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `ownerSegment` read-only property to the `Owner` schema, as a string enum constrained to the four allowed values (`PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`). This generates `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum` at build time, matching the codebase's existing OpenAPI-generated DTO convention (like `ageBand`).\n\n**2. `src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added the derived-field mapping and its method, following the exact pattern of the neighbouring derived fields:\n\n```java\nOwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum ownerSegment(Owner owner) {\n    String tier = membershipLevel(owner) >= 3 ? \"PREMIUM\" : \"STANDARD\";\n    boolean knownRegion = cityRegionResolver.timezoneForRegion(locality(owner)) != null;\n    String area = knownRegion ? \"METRO\" : \"REGIONAL\";\n    return OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum.fromValue(tier + \"_\" + area);\n}\n```\n\n- **TIER** reuses the existing `membershipLevel(owner)` derivation \u2014 `PREMIUM` at level \u2265 3, else `STANDARD`.\n- **AREA** reuses `locality(owner)` (the owner's canonical region) and the resolver's fixed region table \u2014 a region with a known timezone is exactly one of NSW/VIC/QLD, so it maps to `METRO`, otherwise `REGIONAL`. This correctly yields `REGIONAL` for `UNKNOWN` or any non-metro customerCode prefix.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a Sydney/NSW owner, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city) pass.",
